WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.735
-Hello.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.704
Can you see me?

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.973
I'm hiding.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:10.510
I'm gonna be hiding
for the whole episode

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.147
of "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition" tonight.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.984
Let's see if you can --
Oh, did see me move?

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.320
Did you see -- Ah.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.520
Did you see?

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.856
Just kidding.
Hi, everybody.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.959
All-new "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition" starts now.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:27.994
♪♪

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.398
-♪ We in the house ♪
Come on!

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.533
-Tonight join Jimmy
and his guests,

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:38.037
Shailene Woodley, Maluma,

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:42.708
musical guest Thom Yorke,
and the legendary Roots crew.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.811
It's the "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.612
-♪ We in the house, y'all ♪

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:50.249
And now, here's Jimmy.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:53.719
-Hey, everyone, welcome to
"Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.389
This is the hidden episode
because we tried to make

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:00.359
this space into a room where
we might do some jokes from,

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.128
but the acoustics
are pretty bad,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.929
and the lighting isn't great.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:07.066
The wallpaper's great
for what the room normally is

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.501
but not for this.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.836
So we tried to make it look like
a setup, but it's not a setup.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.506
Anyways, so this is kind of
a hidden episode

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:17.143
because we'll never
shoot like this ever again.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:20.246
This will be the first
and last time we broadcast

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.883
from this exact space,
doing exactly this.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.385
So, you found me.
You found the hidden episode.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:30.223
Congratulations.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:33.593
Well, let's get to some jokes
here, everybody.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.728
Costco announced that,
starting next week,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.598
all customers
will have to wear face masks.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.466
It's good 'cause now
you can stay anonymous

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:44.303
while you buy
6 gallons of cheese balls.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.506
I love cheese balls.
-You do.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.074
-What did we get --
We did get them in, like,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.376
a bucket or whatever.
-Every summer. Every summer.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:54.313
-Gosh, it tastes better the more
you -- no one eats them.

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:55.615
-Three months in,
they're even better.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.916
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:00.052
They almost become
a gelatinous cheese ball.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:03.489
-One big ball.
-They become spreadable.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.224
Meanwhile,
a new undercover video

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.126
apparently shows
Home Depot employees

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:11.498
refusing to wear masks at work.
And people are shocked.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:15.068
They said,
"Home Depot has employees?

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.836
Where?

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:20.573
Hello, hello, hello?
I need help, help.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.476
I just don't know where, where
to get, get,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.911
a ball-peen hammer, hammer.

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.714
Anyone work here, here?"

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:32.585
I guess I'll just use
the self check-out, check-out."

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.788
That was my echo training.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.990
I saw that Disney World
is trying to reopen,

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.527
and they're considering
asking guests to wear masks.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.097
It might be necessary
but also takes the fun out of

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.032
seeing a photo of yourself
on the roller coaster

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.101
looking like this.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.139
You got to do a lot of eye work.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:01.714
For the whole time,
because you never know

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.949
when they're gonna take
the flash, either.

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:06.919
They'll still charge you
for that photo, though.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.987
Don't worry about that.

00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:11.490
For the first time ever,
movies that were streaming only

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.894
will now be eligible
for Academy Awards.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.996
They made the switch after
realizing the only movies

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.565
in theaters this year
would've been

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.401
"Sonic the Hedgehog"
and "Dolittle."

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.902
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.672
It was just announced that all
the world's major film festivals

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.640
are going to be consolidated

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:31.911
into one virtual event
that you can view online.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.146
They've even come up
with a catchy name for it --

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:38.484
Netflix.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.119
In a new interview,
Dr. Fauci said,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.389
"We're not ready
for sports to come back yet."

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.424
I don't know.
I think I was ready yesterday

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:51.030
when I watched eight hours of
the World Series of Solitaire.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.332
Well, this is great.
Yesterday, the cast

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.866
of "Melrose Place" reunited

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.102
to raise money
for struggling actors.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.503
Which means all the money raised

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:02.108
will go to the cast
of "Melrose Place."

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.744
I saw that an 11-year-old boy
in Colorado

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.513
caught a trout
the size of a toddler.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.848
At least that's what he said
until his mom was like,

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:13.219
"Ugh.
Please unhook your brother."

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:16.289
I read about a beekeeper
in London who uses the sounds

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:19.458
from his hives
to make electronic music.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.760
So any time you're stressed
during quarantine,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.831
just remember, you could be
living with that guy.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.901
♪ Bzzz, bzzz, bzzz,
bzzz bzzz bzzz, bzzz, bzzz ♪

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:35.407
♪ Bzzz, bzzz bzzz bzzz
bzzz bzzz bzzz bzzz bzzz ♪

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:40.212
♪ Bzzz, bzzz, bzzz,
bzzz, bzzz, bzzz, bzzz ♪

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:43.616
Good.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.584
Finally, I heard about
a group of German doctors

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:47.886
who posed naked online
to raise awareness

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.955
for their lack
of protective equipment.

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:51.190
It taught me two things --

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.693
one, doctors everywhere
need our support.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:57.596
Number two, it's still cold
in Germany in April.

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:58.631
There you guys have it.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.199
That is our monologue
right there.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.466
I appreciate that.

00:05:01.466 --> 00:05:03.235
Thank you
for listening to those.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:04.704
We have a great show tonight.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:08.174
First of all, I wasn't to say
Salesforce is helping us out.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.943
Anything you can donate
to Salesforce between --

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:15.047
Sorry. To World Central Kitchen
between now and June 1st,

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:19.218
Salesforce will match
up to $250,000.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:23.288
So, you can text "meals"
to 80100,

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:24.957
and that will totally help
and totally work.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.692
I think it charges
your phone a dollar.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.727
You can do it really quickly.
You can do it right now.

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:31.497
Have your kids do it.
Show your kids how to donate.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.299
"This is how you do it, kids."

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.568
And, Salesforce,
thanks for stepping up.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.436
That's awesome
that you're doing that.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:38.871
We have a great show tonight.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.774
Shailene Woodley
is on the show tonight.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:45.010
I love talking to Shailene.
Normally, I would --

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.080
You know, I would give her a
hug, and clearly we can't do it.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.249
I don't even know if people
are gonna hug anyone.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.852
But she taught me a cool hug

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.287
for those of you with people
that you can hug.

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:56.888
I can hug you, honey.

00:05:56.888 --> 00:05:58.223
But what she does is,

00:05:58.223 --> 00:06:01.627
she hugs the opposite way,
so our hearts touch.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.396
-Mm.
-That's cute.

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:04.863
And so I've done that
a couple of times --

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:05.897
shown that to
a couple of people.

00:06:05.897 --> 00:06:07.199
They like that.
But that's --

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.001
It always reminds me
of Shailene Woodley.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.903
Also, Maluma.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.604
Gosh, this guy is on fire.

00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:14.106
He's just the biggest
of all big.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:17.109
I love Maluma.
After he did that concert,

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:21.347
by the way,
that we did with Lady Gaga,

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.549
"One World Together At Home,"

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:28.787
his song went to number one
that he did, "Carnival."

00:06:28.787 --> 00:06:33.159
Went to number one,
because he's great.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:36.128
And then, speaking of music --
So check this out.

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:37.630
You're not even gonna
believe this story.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.601
Thom Yorke, from Radiohead --
Thom Yorke --

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.236
was thinking about
what song to do for our show.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:46.972
We love Thom Yorke,
we love Radiohead.

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:51.209
A piece of paper falls out
of his piano thing,

00:06:51.209 --> 00:06:53.646
and it's a song that he --
he didn't know if he was

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:57.283
gonna finish or not.
He finished it for our show.

00:06:57.283 --> 00:07:00.720
"Plasticine Figures."
The debut of the song.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.356
Never been heard
outside of Thom Yorke's brain.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.957
Will be played tonight
for you guys.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:08.961
Thom Yorke, brand-new song,
"Plasticine Figures."

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:11.597
What?
That is the coolest thing ever.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:13.132
I love you, Thom Yorke.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.900
Hey, guys, it's time
for a little thing called

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.536
"What are you Doing Wednesday?"

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:19.271
-♪ What are you doing
this Wednesday? ♪

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:22.808
♪ What are you doing
this Wednesday? ♪

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.410
-This first one here --
a lot of the --

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.912
The first three are dad ones.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:28.881
This first one
is from @shavaunblair.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:31.650
Helps his baby out
with a top-secret mission.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:41.660
♪♪

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:51.670
♪♪

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.973
♪♪

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:56.942
-♪ Doom doom, da-doom-doom ♪

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:59.511
Should you choose to accept it.

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:02.147
This next one is a dad.
He likes to multitask.

00:08:02.147 --> 00:08:05.818
While making dinner,
he has to do other things.

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.854
Watch.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.368
Shh.

00:08:23.368 --> 00:08:25.170
Parent of the Year right there.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.206
I love that move.
Parent of the Year.

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:29.575
That's good.
Cooking and pulling the swing.

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:35.981
This next one is from
@sidevelinbabies.

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:39.151
Her sister told her dad
about her bad grades,

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.920
and her dad came in
and talked to her about.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.154
Watch.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.924
-You had two tests.
-I did them.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.659
-You got a 53 and a 60.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:48.694
You can cheat.
It's online.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.362
-I did cheat!

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:51.530
-And you still got
a 53 and a 60?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.032
-Yes.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:55.935
-No way!
He's the Dad of the Year.

00:08:55.935 --> 00:09:01.040
"Honey, you cheated and still --
Well, cheat better next time.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.208
You cheated and still failed?"

00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:06.011
[ Laughs ]
That's great.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:08.814
This last one here
just kind of made me feel good.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:11.984
It's a neighborhood,
sent from @Laurantfornel,

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.219
posted a video
of her neighborhood

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:16.588
doing a socially distant
line dance.

00:09:16.588 --> 00:09:18.357
It's pretty cool.
Check it out.

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:28.367
♪♪

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:35.174
♪♪

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:37.075
[ Clapping ]
Ah, makes you feel good.

00:09:37.075 --> 00:09:38.777
That is awesome, guys.

00:09:38.777 --> 00:09:41.247
Congrats to everyone who just
joined in and did that.

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.048
That must have been
a cool moment for everyone.

00:09:43.048 --> 00:09:45.184
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:54.393
♪♪

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.394
♪♪

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:58.597
-Two kids coloring together.

00:09:58.597 --> 00:10:01.634
Some friends
celebrating a holiday.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:04.570
Lovers caught in an embrace.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:08.006
An office hard at work.

00:10:08.006 --> 00:10:12.044
A mixed-race family
caught in a candid moment.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:15.681
And a sad boy
looking out of the window.

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:19.652
We may not be able
to make commercials right now,

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:25.023
but we can still make pictures
zoom in and out.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:26.525
Stock images.

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.260
♪♪

